WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:07.980
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:11.770
I hope we have a good time together

00:00:11.770 --> 00:00:15.620
Today let's keep

00:00:17.340 --> 00:00:19.240
Sharing laughs

00:00:19.690 --> 00:00:26.670
You take care of my true wishes in secret

00:00:27.110 --> 00:00:34.220
You always cheer me up after bad days

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:40.580
I'm sure everyone has known it since childhood

00:00:40.980 --> 00:00:49.250
You pretend you don't care, but you're always a good friend

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:58.650
You have another busy day as a god; you just can't help but help out others

00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:04.990
Everyone is cheered up by your love

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:13.300
I love always being together while you help others

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:20.820
I'll protect that precious smile; you know what I mean

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:24.820
When it's a lucky day with nice weather

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:28.400
We should go visit the shrine together

00:02:00.440 --> 00:02:03.860
Like always, this place is boring
since it's secluded in the mountains.

00:02:07.350 --> 00:02:11.770
Mayu-sama, you didn't have to come
with me if you didn't want to.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:19.880
TL Note: Yomotsu Hirasaka is the road down to the underworld.

00:02:15.310 --> 00:02:19.880
If I miss this chance, the next time I
meet him might be in Yomotsu Hirasaka.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:20.590
Oh my.

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:23.960
I heard that, you stray cat!

00:02:23.960 --> 00:02:27.220
Master, did you come all the way here to pick me up?!

00:02:27.220 --> 00:02:29.740
Long time no see, Yuzu.

00:02:29.740 --> 00:02:31.280
And...

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:32.650
I guess you too, Mayu.

00:02:41.430 --> 00:02:47.060
Master, I'm sorry I couldn't even see you on New Year's.

00:02:47.060 --> 00:02:49.690
Don't worry about it.

00:02:49.690 --> 00:02:54.290
I know you're busy taking care
of the shop and that stray cat.

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.920
It seems you're as rude as ever.

00:02:57.800 --> 00:03:01.550
By the way, Yuzu, you can stop calling me Master.

00:03:02.500 --> 00:03:06.050
You've become more of an expert
on antiques than I ever was.

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.310
Just call me Jiichan like you used to.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:16.560
Sure, Genzou-ojiichan!

00:03:19.910 --> 00:03:28.870
This clear sky reminds me of the day you first showed up, Stray Cat.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:34.710
Are you going senile, Geezer? That day was
completely different; it was gloomy and raining.

00:03:35.210 --> 00:03:36.810
It definitely wasn't raining.

00:03:36.810 --> 00:03:38.760
Actually, it <i>was  raining.</i>

00:03:38.760 --> 00:03:40.400
Okay, it might have been raining.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.250
What's up with the different reactions?!

00:03:43.680 --> 00:03:45.670
I'm very sure of it.

00:03:45.670 --> 00:03:50.260
It was in the middle of a long rainy season.

00:04:01.950 --> 00:04:05.240
They look kind of gloomy today.

00:04:08.750 --> 00:04:10.250
Do we have a guest?

00:04:13.890 --> 00:04:15.460
Why are <i>they  here?</i>

00:04:21.370 --> 00:04:23.800
We've been waiting for you.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:27.310
I assume you're Saeki Genzou-san, the potter.

00:04:27.310 --> 00:04:30.800
Who are you? What do you want with me?

00:04:30.800 --> 00:04:32.980
Oh, we should've introduced ourselves first.

00:04:33.480 --> 00:04:38.990
I work as an antique dealer in Tokyo. My name is Katou.

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:45.910
President of the Art Scope Corporation, Katou Shuuji-san, eh?

00:04:46.500 --> 00:04:48.250
Why are you here—

00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:48.250
Please go away!

00:04:49.330 --> 00:04:50.750
Yuzu!

00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:52.770
Oh, that is—

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:56.510
Katou-san, I've already turned down your offer.

00:04:56.510 --> 00:05:00.520
Now you're intruding upon Genzou-ojiichan's place!

00:05:01.670 --> 00:05:06.140
Komiya Yuzu-san, I didn't know
you were here too. I'm in luck...

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.140
or maybe not.

00:05:11.780 --> 00:05:13.560
I'll visit again.

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:19.390
What was that about?

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.570
Oh, I see.

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:29.340
I more or less understand what that Katou guy was doing.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:38.800
You bluntly denied his offers, so he
came to see me, your guardian.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:43.050
He keeps pestering me to sell the
antiques my dad left behind.

00:05:43.690 --> 00:05:51.020
I mentioned your name because he was nagging so
much, but I never expected him to actually come here.

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:55.370
I'm sorry!

00:05:55.370 --> 00:06:01.360
You don't have to apologize, Yuzu.
You haven't done anything wrong.

00:06:01.360 --> 00:06:02.570
Okay.

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:08.520
Let's set that aside for now and discuss
who that midget is over there.

00:06:08.520 --> 00:06:09.530
I'm a goddess!

00:06:09.530 --> 00:06:11.280
Or so she claims.

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:16.640
This odd girl is a goddess, huh?

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:18.680
Wait, are you doubting me?

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:20.630
No, not really.

00:06:20.630 --> 00:06:24.570
Even a stone worshiped in a shrine is called a god.

00:06:24.570 --> 00:06:26.800
That bothers me even more.

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:34.310
So, you're saying this "goddess" has nowhere to go and that you want her to stay at Yaoyorozu-dou, right?

00:06:34.310 --> 00:06:37.780
Well, it's not like I have nowhere else to...

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:41.820
nowhere else to go...

00:06:44.360 --> 00:06:49.040
Um, I'd like to let Mayu-sama continue living at my home.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:54.070
Well, you're free to keep what you wish, be it a cat or a goddess.

00:06:54.070 --> 00:06:54.950
Y-Yes.

00:06:55.450 --> 00:07:05.960
I'm acting as your guardian because you have no relatives,
but that shop and the house belong to you and no one else.

00:07:05.960 --> 00:07:10.310
Now then, I guess I'll start preparing dinner.

00:07:11.470 --> 00:07:14.470
Guys, what would you like to eat?

00:07:15.200 --> 00:07:17.600
U-Um, Genzou-ojiichan...

00:07:18.430 --> 00:07:20.480
I have another request.

00:07:20.480 --> 00:07:22.230
Hm? What is it?

00:07:23.310 --> 00:07:27.770
Um, can you teach me about antiques?

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:29.920
What's gotten into you?

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:33.400
If you want to negotiate with Katou, I can do it on your behalf—

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.270
This doesn't have anything to do with him!

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:38.260
I just...

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:41.780
I want to succeed my parents!

00:07:43.060 --> 00:07:45.280
What?!

00:07:46.360 --> 00:07:48.300
A test?

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.290
Yes...

00:07:49.980 --> 00:07:55.290
I've always said that I'm against you inheriting that shop.

00:07:56.650 --> 00:08:04.400
You're good at academics and pretty to boot, but most of all, you're still young with many possibilities open to you.

00:08:04.400 --> 00:08:09.310
You think antiques are what you want to do in life, but your passion might not last.

00:08:09.820 --> 00:08:13.060
You don't need to solidify your future just yet.

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:20.820
If you still want to learn from me, you'll have to show me that you're a student worth teaching.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.470
The test instructions are simple.

00:08:26.470 --> 00:08:30.090
Lying here is a part of my old ceramics collection.

00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:38.000
They're all masterpieces with certification or have been appraised by a connoisseur, but counterfeit pieces are also mixed among them.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:40.620
You have to figure out which ones are counterfeit.

00:09:01.860 --> 00:09:03.850
The third and fifth ones from the right.

00:09:05.920 --> 00:09:11.650
Also... the celadon pot on the far left is half-counterfeit that's been fired twice.

00:09:15.070 --> 00:09:16.370
That is correct.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:21.660
After all, you've been observing antiques since
you were little. You've developed a good eye.

00:09:21.660 --> 00:09:22.980
Do I pass?

00:09:22.980 --> 00:09:26.060
No, the next question is the true test.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:32.720
Which one of these do you think has the highest value?

00:09:35.870 --> 00:09:39.390
I have no idea about antiques' market prices.

00:09:40.770 --> 00:09:44.960
That gold lacquer plate looks very appealing, but it's fake.

00:09:44.960 --> 00:09:48.900
Although, just because it's fake doesn't mean it doesn't have value.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:58.330
This Shigaraki ware has a very nice surface quality and I like it, but it's nothing special and was made recently by a no-name.

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:04.650
I don't know.

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:07.230
You fail.

00:10:15.520 --> 00:10:18.210
I wonder how I should have answered.

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:29.130
Now that I think about it, I love antiques and old ceramics, but I've never considered their monetary value before.

00:10:30.170 --> 00:10:34.950
Maybe Genzou-ojiichan saw through that.

00:10:40.190 --> 00:10:43.760
So, what was the correct answer?

00:10:43.760 --> 00:10:54.990
Oh yeah, I paid the most for the big plate third from the left, but the old ceramics never hold their value.

00:10:57.340 --> 00:11:00.110
There's no correct answer really.

00:11:00.110 --> 00:11:04.140
What?! Are you saying you tricked Yuzu?

00:11:04.140 --> 00:11:05.120
Oh?

00:11:10.240 --> 00:11:13.010
It's interesting you got angry on Yuzu's behalf.

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:18.010
I-It's not like I got angry for her sake.

00:11:18.840 --> 00:11:22.510
It's just, since I'm a goddess, I can't let a foul play like that slide.

00:11:22.510 --> 00:11:29.020
Say, if you're really a goddess, can you protect Yuzu?

00:11:30.710 --> 00:11:34.780
Even if I wanted to, my divine powers aren't that strong.

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.310
That doesn't really matter.

00:11:37.310 --> 00:11:40.890
By the way, what are you the goddess of?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:45.460
I-I...

00:11:45.650 --> 00:11:49.370
I'm not sure what goddess I am.

00:11:51.640 --> 00:11:55.870
I'll eat sashimi to my heart's content once this fight's over!

00:12:06.120 --> 00:12:07.880
Oh, Komiya Yuzu-san.

00:12:08.380 --> 00:12:11.530
Why the long face? Is something wrong?

00:12:11.530 --> 00:12:13.090
It's none of your business.

00:12:13.510 --> 00:12:15.960
That was harsh.

00:12:15.960 --> 00:12:17.220
By the way, that—

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.100
I won't change my mind!

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:27.630
Yuzu-san, I understand your attachment to the shop's items as mementos of your late father.

00:12:27.630 --> 00:12:35.120
However, I doubt your father would want you to lock up all those antiques as keepsakes.

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:40.120
You aren't going to succeed the shop, are you?

00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.750
Please excuse me.

00:12:43.370 --> 00:12:46.820
Oh no, I think I made her cry.

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:50.130
Does that mean she wants to inherit the shop then?

00:12:50.660 --> 00:12:54.810
You know that's impossible. She can't become an antiques dealer.

00:12:54.810 --> 00:12:59.960
It takes talent and years of training
to cultivate an eye for antiques.

00:12:59.960 --> 00:13:03.500
You're in this business yourself, so I'm sure you know.

00:13:03.500 --> 00:13:05.940
That might be true, but still...

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:08.650
Excuse me.

00:13:10.130 --> 00:13:11.780
Yes!

00:13:11.780 --> 00:13:12.800
Yes.

00:13:14.420 --> 00:13:18.230
All right, we'll go pick it up today.

00:13:20.410 --> 00:13:21.410
Thanks.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:25.080
The you-know-what's are ready to go.

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:25.920
I see.

00:13:26.530 --> 00:13:28.350
President.

00:13:28.350 --> 00:13:31.140
Um, are we really doing this?

00:13:31.140 --> 00:13:32.870
Yes, we'll strike tonight.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.180
But this is a crime.

00:13:35.610 --> 00:13:39.440
I don't care. I'll be buying all of them at some point.

00:13:39.440 --> 00:13:43.180
I'm just going a little out of order.
The gods should be fine with that.

00:14:06.840 --> 00:14:09.710
It should be right here.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.500
Absolutely wonderful!

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:21.800
As one would expect from a living legend, Fujita Ryuuji.

00:14:30.590 --> 00:14:36.930
I went out of my way to have this counterfeit made, but it pales in comparison to the real thing.

00:14:36.930 --> 00:14:40.280
That little girl won't be able to tell, though.

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.480
Stop right there, burglar.

00:14:43.230 --> 00:14:44.790
Give up and behave yourself.

00:14:44.790 --> 00:14:46.700
Shit!

00:14:46.700 --> 00:14:50.640
Should I run away? She hasn't seen my face yet.

00:14:50.640 --> 00:14:54.300
No, if I run, the precious ceramic might get fractured.

00:14:54.300 --> 00:14:57.850
Very good, it looks like you've given up.

00:14:57.850 --> 00:14:59.800
Turn around slowly.

00:15:03.160 --> 00:15:05.060
G-Good evening!

00:15:06.140 --> 00:15:10.340
You're that Katou guy who's been nagging Yuzu recently!

00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:14.100
I didn't know you'd resort to this, miserable scum!

00:15:14.100 --> 00:15:16.570
Yuzu, I caught the burglar!

00:15:16.570 --> 00:15:20.900
Katou-san, why would you do such a thing?!

00:15:22.100 --> 00:15:25.280
Yuzu-san, I'm at a loss for what to do.

00:15:26.080 --> 00:15:30.830
Goodness, what did you come to steal? I'm going to inspect this.

00:15:30.450 --> 00:15:31.210
H-Hey!

00:15:31.210 --> 00:15:33.460
Don't be so rough with it.

00:15:33.460 --> 00:15:35.140
A tea bowl?

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.630
I can't believe you'd become a thief for something like this.

00:15:38.740 --> 00:15:40.550
That's Fujita Ryuuji's!

00:15:40.550 --> 00:15:42.790
Perfect, that's the counterfeit.

00:15:44.030 --> 00:15:47.730
Yuzu-san, can you let me go just this once?

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:51.840
I'll even do you a favor in return for your grace.

00:15:51.840 --> 00:15:56.730
I'll give that back, and I'll pay sufficient compensation.

00:15:56.730 --> 00:16:01.870
This sounds fishy. What exactly are you plotting?

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:04.870
There's another one!

00:16:06.720 --> 00:16:08.250
A duplicate?

00:16:08.250 --> 00:16:11.620
He must have tried to switch the real one with a fake!

00:16:11.620 --> 00:16:13.630
We'll be keeping both of these.

00:16:13.630 --> 00:16:16.880
No, that'd be a problem.

00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:21.630
One of them is Yuzu-san's, but the other one is mine.

00:16:21.630 --> 00:16:24.490
You have to choose one.

00:16:24.490 --> 00:16:26.930
I can choose for you if you'd like.

00:16:26.930 --> 00:16:30.260
Th-That's ridiculous! What an impudent burglar!

00:16:30.260 --> 00:16:31.420
Mayu-sama...

00:16:40.920 --> 00:16:42.770
Yuzu-san, how about this?

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:47.280
If you can't choose one, I'm willing to buy both of them.

00:16:47.670 --> 00:16:50.940
Yuzu, don't listen to this rogue's blithering nonsense!

00:16:50.940 --> 00:16:52.040
Have him arrested this instant!

00:16:52.670 --> 00:16:55.460
Katou-san, please keep talking.

00:16:55.460 --> 00:16:57.130
Excellent, she took the bait.

00:16:58.630 --> 00:16:59.380
Yuzu!

00:16:59.920 --> 00:17:03.800
I'll pay a total of three million yen for both of them.

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.300
What do you say? It's not a bad deal, is it?

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:24.850
Mayu-sama, could you put both of
these back into Katou-san's bag?

00:17:24.850 --> 00:17:28.000
Yuzu, are you really going to take his offer?

00:17:28.490 --> 00:17:30.540
A wise decision.

00:17:30.540 --> 00:17:35.170
Katou-san, I don't mind if you take both of them,

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:37.930
and I don't need the three million yen either.

00:17:40.270 --> 00:17:46.640
However, you'll have to give back my real tea bowl that you hid in your chest pocket!

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:49.960
Don't tell me this guy...

00:17:53.720 --> 00:17:55.500
Is that the real one?!

00:17:55.750 --> 00:17:58.760
He prepared two counterfeits?!

00:17:59.440 --> 00:18:04.010
She realized both of them were counterfeit this quickly.

00:18:04.690 --> 00:18:06.800
This girl is something else.

00:18:06.800 --> 00:18:07.510
Katou-san...

00:18:08.930 --> 00:18:15.570
Antiques were torn apart from their owners because of various reasons, weren't they?

00:18:16.350 --> 00:18:21.580
Some of them were locked up dark storage
rooms, while others lay forgotten inside boxes.

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:34.090
My dad said an antique seller's job is to bring the antiques out into the light again and find them new owners.

00:18:35.620 --> 00:18:40.600
Look, Yuzu. This pot right here was left
abandoned for over two hundred years.

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:45.610
But, as you can see, it's finally found a new owner to stay with.

00:18:45.610 --> 00:18:47.350
That's great, Dad!

00:18:47.350 --> 00:18:48.860
Yeah, it's great.

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:58.370
Dad hand-picked and bought each and every one of the items here.

00:18:58.880 --> 00:19:12.130
I want to reopen Yaoyorozu-dou someday and when I do,
I want to find every antique my dad collected a new owner.

00:19:12.980 --> 00:19:14.130
Yuzu!

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:18.370
I had it all wrong.

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:22.140
This girl is undoubtedly the real deal.

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.870
Now, call the police.

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:30.480
No, I don't intend to report this to the police.

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:35.990
Instead... I have a favor to ask you.

00:19:45.120 --> 00:19:48.840
Oh, is it finally a sunny day after all the rain?

00:19:52.500 --> 00:19:54.630
That car is...

00:19:56.450 --> 00:20:01.140
Good morning, Saeki Genzou-san.
I came here today with a request.

00:20:01.740 --> 00:20:05.380
It's useless to try coercing Yuzu through me.

00:20:05.380 --> 00:20:07.640
She's stubborn despite her looks.

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:09.900
Oh, no, that's already taken care of.

00:20:10.380 --> 00:20:16.650
Saeki-san, would you give us permission
to handle your ceramic works?

00:20:18.430 --> 00:20:20.910
You can decide the price.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:23.280
What are you up to?

00:20:23.670 --> 00:20:27.790
Well, I'm not up to anything, but I do have another request.

00:20:29.430 --> 00:20:36.670
Saeki-san, can you please help me teach
her the basics of antique selling?

00:20:36.670 --> 00:20:37.550
"Her"?

00:20:39.300 --> 00:20:42.550
Wait, what is going on here?

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:49.810
Please, I'm asking you again, Genzou-ojii—

00:20:50.390 --> 00:20:51.310
I mean...

00:20:52.950 --> 00:20:54.520
Master!

00:20:55.810 --> 00:21:05.330
I see. Yuzu's smile that day made such a huge impression on me that I forgot all about the gloomy rain.

00:21:08.800 --> 00:21:11.770
Did he finally go senile? He's laughing at himself.

00:21:11.770 --> 00:21:13.190
Mayu-sama!

00:21:14.550 --> 00:21:16.340
Genzou-ojiichan...

00:21:16.710 --> 00:21:19.970
I went to the beach with Mayu-sama and her friends.

00:21:19.970 --> 00:21:20.840
Here's a souvenir.

00:21:24.290 --> 00:21:26.350
Barnacle Acorn Buns!

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:28.400
They're very delicious!

00:21:28.400 --> 00:21:31.820
Look, it's filled up on the inside of the lid too!

00:21:31.820 --> 00:21:32.810
Thank you.

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:34.160
You're welcome!

00:21:34.160 --> 00:21:36.570
I'll prepare dinner tonight.

00:21:45.730 --> 00:21:49.080
Your daughter...

00:21:49.080 --> 00:21:51.330
just gets me every time.

00:21:52.500 --> 00:21:54.350
Don't you agree, Makitarou?

00:22:02.140 --> 00:22:09.190
I gently peered into the future which we call tomorrow

00:22:09.190 --> 00:22:13.290
Looking at the world upside down

00:22:13.320 --> 00:22:20.350
I projected my memories upon the glittering cotton candy clouds

00:22:20.360 --> 00:22:24.460
And hung rainbow ribbons

00:22:24.480 --> 00:22:31.780
When I'm left alone, I feel lonely and depressed

00:22:32.190 --> 00:22:38.250
So stay here forever

00:22:38.250 --> 00:22:43.490
I'm sure everyone has some

00:22:43.490 --> 00:22:49.400
Unfulfilled desires locked inside their hearts

00:22:51.660 --> 00:23:01.610
I want you to realize that small memory that won't disappear is the key. Yeah

00:23:01.610 --> 00:23:08.080
You're always the only one

00:23:08.080 --> 00:23:12.370
Who can make me reminisce fondly

00:23:26.400 --> 00:23:41.370
Next Episode

00:23:27.540 --> 00:23:31.150
Yuzu, you know how there are sometimes
trivial things that bother people?

00:23:31.150 --> 00:23:36.190
Mayu-sama, you look like you're bothered by
something, but it's probably trivial so I won't ask.

00:23:36.190 --> 00:23:37.880
Oh, was it <i>that</i> obvious that I wanted to talk to you?

00:23:37.880 --> 00:23:38.410
Yes.

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Nezametsuki Thriller Night

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.370
Nezametsuki Thriller Night

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:41.420
The next episode will be a festival at Gonta-san's shrine!
